+            /* Sanity cap only. The old cap here was 0x7FFFFE00 (~2GB) on the
+             * theory that "blk_pread uses a signed 32-bit count" — but
+             * blk_pread takes int64_t bytes (block-backend-io.h); only its
+             * RETURN is int, and we read in 64MB chunks, so the total size was
+             * never the constraint. The real 2GB bug was `int size =
+             * blk_getlength()` overflowing, fixed separately with int64_t.
+             *
+             * NOTE: vdisk_ram is anonymous host RAM of exactly this size, so a
+             * 3GB disk costs 3GB of host memory. Cap generously but finitely
+             * so a corrupt VTOC cannot ask for a terabyte. */
+            disk_size = MIN(disk_size, (int64_t)64 * 1024 * 1024 * 1024);
+            if (disk_size <= 0)
